   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. The main points I settled were:\n\n- **Left end:** a 3-amino-6-(2-hydroxyphenyl)pyridazin-4-yl group is attached to N3 of a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane. N8 of that bicycle is bonded to C4 of a pyridine, which carries an O-linked substituent at C2.\n- **Cyclobutane linker:** the two ether oxygens on the 1,3-disubstituted cyclobutane are drawn one wedged and one hashed, so I wrote them as trans. This is a cis/trans relationship only, because the ring has no true stereocentres.\n- **Middle:** the cyclobutane is linked through O to C4 of a piperidine. The piperidine N carries a CH2CH2O chain leading to C3 of an isoxazole.\n- **Isoxazole side chain:** C5 of the isoxazole bears a CH(isopropyl)C(=O) group. The isopropyl is hashed, and working out the CIP priorities gives S at this carbon.\n- **Right end:** the C(=O) is bonded to the N of a 4-hydroxypyrrolidine-2-carboxamide. I read the hashed OH and wedged carbonyl as the usual (2S,4R) VHL-ligand arrangement and used the standard SMILES pattern for it.\n- **Terminal amide:** the amide N is attached to a CH bearing a CHF2 group (wedged) and a phenyl ring. The ring has a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl substituent. Working out the priorities gives R at this carbon.\n\nI checked the ring-closure labels for reuse and the atom counts by hand against the drawing.\n\nSMILES: Nc1nnc(-c2ccccc2O)cc1N1CC2CCC(C1)N2c1ccnc(O[C@H]2C[C@H](OC3CCN(CCOc4cc(on4)[C@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N4C[C@H](O)C[C@H]4C(=O)N[C@H](c4ccc(-c5scnc5C)cc4)C(F)F)CC3)C2)c1"
